@startuml keycloak-sequence-full-flow
!theme plain

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam participant {
    BackgroundColor #B4D7E8
    BorderColor #8B9DC3
}
skinparam actor {
    BackgroundColor #E0BBE4
    BorderColor #C8A4D4
}
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #8B9DC3
    LifeLineBorderColor #8B9DC3
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #F0F0F0
}
skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor #FFF4CD
    BorderColor #E6D5AC
}

scale 0.3

title Keycloak Authentication Flow - Authorization Code + PKCE\n(Full Flow with JWT Validation)

actor User
participant "Browser\n(SPA)" as Browser
participant "Keycloak\nServer" as Keycloak
participant "Backend\n(API)" as Backend

autonumber

== Authentication Phase ==

User -> Browser: Click Login

Browser -> Browser: Generate PKCE\n• code_verifier\n• code_challenge\n(S256 hash)

Browser -> Keycloak: Redirect to Authorization Endpoint\n• code_challenge\n• client_id: frontend-spa\n• redirect_uri\n• response_type: code\n• scope: openid profile email

Keycloak -> User: Present Login Screen

User -> Keycloak: Enter Credentials\n(username/password)

Keycloak -> Keycloak: Validate Credentials

Keycloak -> Browser: Return Authorization Code\n(redirect to callback URI)

Browser -> Keycloak: Exchange Code for Tokens\nPOST /token\n• code\n• code_verifier\n• client_id\n• grant_type: authorization_code

Keycloak -> Keycloak: Verify PKCE\n(code_challenge matches\ncode_verifier)

Keycloak -> Browser: Return Tokens:\n• access_token (JWT)\n• refresh_token\n• id_token

Browser -> Browser: Store tokens in memory\n(not localStorage)

Browser -> User: User Authenticated\n(display logged-in state)

== API Access Phase ==

User -> Browser: Request API Data

Browser -> Backend: API Call\nGET /api/data\nAuthorization: Bearer <access_token>

Backend -> Keycloak: Fetch JWKS\n(first time or cached)

Keycloak -> Backend: Public Keys\n(RSA key pairs)

Backend -> Backend: Validate JWT:\n• Signature (JWKS)\n• Issuer\n• Expiry (exp)\n• Audience (aud)\n• Not Before (nbf)

Backend -> Backend: Extract Claims:\n• Roles\n• Scopes\n• Permissions

Backend -> Backend: Authorize:\nCheck user has\nrequired roles\n(@PreAuthorize)

Backend -> Browser: API Response\n200 OK\n{ data }

Browser -> User: Display Data

note over Browser, Backend
    All API requests include:
    Authorization: Bearer <access_token>

    Token stored in memory only
    (cleared on page refresh/logout)
end note

footer Keycloak 26.5.7 | Authorization Code + PKCE Flow | Generated: April 7, 2026

@enduml

